Reading: (A) and (B) are observational axiom sets (only e, s0, s1, R, =) whose models contain
unnamed pair elements; they reproduce the alternating-machine and the finite-theory constructions
that short-derivations Props 4.3 and 4.12 build with theoretical symbols C, C', pr.  (C) shows the
other side: finite theories true in the free term model (only named objects) fit regular languages,
by the signature construction; that they fit nothing else is Prop 3.12 (Rabin), not computed here.
